  </div>
  <div class="community-details"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SIMPLE WAY TO BEGIN</p><h2>A notebook with an open door.</h2><p>The conversation starts in this site’s GitHub issues. You can read public threads without signing in; posting needs a GitHub account. Each button opens a draft for you to review and submit. Nothing is sent by this website.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/jsdyer/jsd-technologies/issues">Read the public question board <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></div><div><p class="eyebrow">GOOD NEIGHBOUR RULES</p><ul><li>Describe the problem, your environment and what you tried.</li><li>Keep it kind, practical and within systems you’re allowed to work on.</li><li>Remove passwords, tokens, personal details and private hostnames from examples.</li><li>Only share text, code and images you have permission to publish.</li></ul><p>Prefer email? <a class="text-link" href="mailto:jeffdyer@gmail.com?subject=Workshop%20question">Write to Jeffrey</a>. Contributions are reviewed before they become site content; replies and publication aren’t guaranteed.</p></div></div>
